description: Tool-agnostic AGENT_HANDOFF.md rotation protocol shared across Claude Code, OpenCode, and Cursor
alwaysApply: true
---

The handoff lifecycle uses a hybrid pattern: a thin `.ai/AGENT_HANDOFF.md` for the current
task and an append-only `.ai/TASK_LOG.md` archive. A shared Node engine,
`.ai/scripts/rotate-handoff.mjs`, is the single source of truth for rotation across Claude
Code, OpenCode, and Cursor.

## When to rotate

Rotate when the human marks the current task done in `.ai/AGENT_HANDOFF.md` and confirms the
task is complete (verification passed, no remaining work).

## How to rotate (Cursor)

Run from the integrated terminal:

```bash
node .ai/scripts/rotate-handoff.mjs
```

The script will:

1. Append the current `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` to `TASK_LOG.md` with an ISO-timestamp separator.
2. Rotate `TASK_LOG.md` into `.ai/archive/TASK_LOG-YYYY-MM.md` if it exceeds 500 lines.
3. Overwrite `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` with a clean scaffold.

Then re-read `AGENT_HANDOFF.md`, fill in the next task's title, goal, non-goals, branch, and
base branch, and confirm with the human before implementation.

## What not to do

- Do not hand-edit `TASK_LOG.md` or files under `.ai/archive/`.
- Do not append new tasks on top of an old `AGENT_HANDOFF.md`; that defeats the
  context-window budget.
- Do not bypass the script with manual file moves; it keeps separators and rotation thresholds
  consistent across tools.

The full protocol and rationale are in `.ai/HARNESS.md` "Handoff Protocol (Tool-Agnostic)".
